cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Finite Game Equilibria: exhaustive pure-strategy equilibrium checks for explicit finite games"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/finite-game-equilibria"
abstract: >-
  Standard-library Python checker that enumerates every joint-action profile
  of an explicitly supplied finite game, reports each player's best unilateral
  deviation, and returns all pure-strategy epsilon-Nash equilibria. Pure
  strategies only (no mixed equilibria); cost grows as the product of the
  action counts. Strict input validation and JSON-safe output. No claims
  beyond the supplied payoff table.
keywords:
  - "game-theory"
  - "nash-equilibrium"
  - "pure-strategy"
  - "finite-games"
  - "epsilon-equilibrium"
  - "python"
references:
